{"title":"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two parabolas have equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f526f7c478299df74c73c277b90621d967b56c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y= x^2 + ax +b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b5ee5ff6e082f8b985aea208de9a59ba786f332.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y= x^2 + cx +d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d02bb2275100261109b043261e702124460a83e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are integers, each chosen independently by rolling a fair six-sided die. What is the probability that the parabolas will have at least one point in common?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550286a21404244c7e02ccb3e1894435f8a99354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{25}{36}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{5}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{31}{36}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"382\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Set the two equations equal to each other: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69ea346be3a60bf0e89884fb60cb092f483bb2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + ax + b = x^2 + cx + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"206\" height=\"18\" />. Now remove the x squared and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />'s on one side: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb69196c885894c90a2d63e458cc211196c3ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax-cx=d-b$\" width=\"124\" height=\"12\" />. Now factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/258be19b1cf5f4daa87ed005045d0e868d7b0270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(a-c)=d-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, then there is always a solution, but if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f717c40ef1d78faf6efbaef5c9e6f804d544faf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=c$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" />, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> chance, leaving a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f16fb84a8ee112a4dbb09e361549f8cb2696725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1080$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d12e688b849bdc599794d49762ec2d6fb3583b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1296$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, always having at least one point in common. And if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f717c40ef1d78faf6efbaef5c9e6f804d544faf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=c$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" />, then the only way for that to work, is if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db7c484eabfd9c6a0df50467667bf3658e63b815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=b$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> chance, however, this can occur <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways, so a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> chance of this happening. So adding one  thirty sixth to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f97d5a3842441a4aea8e3841081b4f25bc47fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1080}{1296}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />, we get the simplified fraction of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c253211ed5a85ce23173963862b801e5bad8284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{31}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />; answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de641a309fc5878c26baf699f2382b7d4b02b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Proceed as above to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/258be19b1cf5f4daa87ed005045d0e868d7b0270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(a-c)=d-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />. The probability that the parabolas have at least 1 point in common is 1 minus the probability that they do not intersect. The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/258be19b1cf5f4daa87ed005045d0e868d7b0270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(a-c)=d-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> has no solution if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f717c40ef1d78faf6efbaef5c9e6f804d544faf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=c$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a24be171191f46bc2198359cff964ebfee201b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\neq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f717c40ef1d78faf6efbaef5c9e6f804d544faf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=c$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> while the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a24be171191f46bc2198359cff964ebfee201b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\neq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/5533bc48602603f16d18c04858cad119c04833c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79cac78d2a5a9b666875d7b6de755bc67bab5aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)=\\frac{31}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"157\" height=\"43\" /> for the probability that the parabolas intersect.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e306774c5ff626516b9868a0f8b00dc056a7f1e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax + b = cx + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"124\" height=\"14\" />. Imagine the two sides as lines - they will have no solutions when the two lines are parallel (eg. have the same gradient) which is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Also, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc4f1e0e90e5a512db1597847079ee19aad2541a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = d$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0baced26dbcf8c61bff7cd5d6ab63bb3917e0ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = c$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" />, they're the same line so we must add one case. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> combinations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, of which they are equal in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> - but we must subtract 1 as if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f717c40ef1d78faf6efbaef5c9e6f804d544faf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=c$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d842008346c10aa7b9e064b41b75d4e4e4e4427d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=d$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> they still intersect and have solutions. So we subtract this to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/8311a93fd3a966b13fadb352ee4c855dfa311c87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36}{36} - \\frac{5}{36} = \\frac{31}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>~ youtube.com/indianmathguy\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/9/479a33a6c4df17d3abb496852d160a6be629aac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+ax+b=(x+ \\frac{a}{2})^2+b- \\frac{a^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"257\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6fb6eb7b6c2ba443702564006a228452c43276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+cx+d=(x+ \\frac{c}{2})^2+d- \\frac{c^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"257\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>The only case where these two functions have no intersections is when the x-values of the turning point are the same but the y-values are not the same.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9cec832c49717e66decbec5b07ebf52a5e3ed3c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\therefore \\frac{a}{2}= \\frac{c}{2} \\implies a=c \\quad\\quad probability = \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{1}{6} \\times 6= \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"422\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7ee5ba3e19cf68e2320ad0ec4c7e6eba1c8d5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b- \\frac{a^2}{4} \\neq d- \\frac{c^2}{4} \\implies b \\neq d \\quad\\quad probability = 1- \\frac{1}{6}\\times \\frac{1}{6}\\times 6= \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"511\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07f2e24a52db7043b582c74af25d38189a6ffe3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\therefore 1- \\frac{1}{6}\\times \\frac{5}{6} = 1- \\frac{5}{36} = \\frac{31}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"223\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~ JiYang\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&a